SOAPBOX: Perhaps the worst conditions that I remember.
SOAPBOX: No WA, WY or NV. OR and MT the last morning.
SOAPBOX: Small participation, with very few signals over 1845.
SOAPBOX: Strong but deaf PP5 the first evening and
SOAPBOX: always present KH6AQ.
SOAPBOX: I set up a bent vertical to a 120' tower with just
SOAPBOX: 8 60' radials. A week earlier that vertical was a few db better
SOAPBOX: to EU than my 100' shunt tower so I had high hopes but the EU
SOAPBOX: propagation was short.
SOAPBOX: Due to very dry weather lots of powerline static this time.
SOAPBOX: Upgrade of Flex 6600 from version 3 to 4 was a big mistake as the
SOAPBOX: new version has a galore of bugs. A few crashes, frequent interlock
SOAPBOX: and "reduce power messages" and weird key. Also untunable APF and
SOAPBOX: NB that creates many false signals.
